# Fedora

These are dependency pointers, not verified Fedora installation steps. The
current CI workflow does not build on Fedora; see `INSTALL` for the tested CI
configurations. Package names can vary by Fedora release. For a source build,
install development packages for CMake 3.10+, C and C++ compilers, Bison 3.0+, Flex,
GnuTLS, libgcrypt, libidn2, pkg-config, and SCTP (unless building with
`-DDISABLE_SCTP=ON`).

Optional extension dependencies include PostgreSQL development files for
`app_acct`, MySQL development files for `app_sip` and `app_diameap`, libxml2
development files for `dict_legacy_xml`, and Python 3 development files plus
SWIG for `dbg_interactive`.

Do not disable SELinux to work around a bind or policy denial. Diagnose the
specific denial and configure an appropriately scoped policy for the service
and ports in use.
